<title>SOUTH KOREA: Hyundai wins Singapore subway contract.</title>
<headline>Hyundai wins Singapore subway contract.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Hyundai Engineering and Construction Co Ltd and Zueblin AG of Germany have won a $222.54 million order to build a 20 km section of railway for the Singapore subway, a Hyundai statement said on Friday.</p>
<p>Hyundai's share of the contract is worth $159.4 million and Zueblin's $63.14 million, the statement said. The two companies will jointly manage the turnkey project.</p>
<p>The new line, to be completed by April 2002, will link the World Trade Centre to the district of Punggol.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
